# Exoplanet Transit Detection

Detects transiting exoplanets in Kepler/TESS light curves using the
Box Least Squares (BLS) algorithm, recovering known planets as a
validation check.

## Method
1. Download light curve data via `lightkurve` (MAST)
2. Clean & flatten to remove stellar variability
3. Run BLS to search for periodic transit signals
4. Fold at best period, compare to published parameters

## Status
🚧 Week 1-2 in progress — data pipeline + BLS search working on Kepler-10b

## Setup
\`\`\`bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
